  "semantics": {
    "text": "# Gauge@1 semantics\n\nThe capability package for digital hand gauges and indicators: calipers, micrometers, dial and digital indicators, height, bore and depth gauges, and protractors.\n\n- Describe and configuration come from Device@1; the driver reports the gauge kind, range and resolution (GaugeInfo) with describe. The package has no core settings: any setting is a vendor extension under a namespace listed in describe.\n- read returns one reading now. zero makes the present position read zero. Both are D1. No operation writes calibration, and zero leaves the calibration reference unchanged.\n- start_stream, stop_stream and stream_status come from the shared streaming template. A stream delivers gauge-batch/1 batches with one sequence number per reading. Lengths use the gauge.readings batch schema and angles gauge.readings.angle.\n- A reading carries the value in m or rad, the resolution in the same unit, the gauge identity, an optional calibration reference (a digest of the calibration record), optional t_dev and required t_host in ns. The value is an integer multiple of the resolution within 1e-9 relative.\n- A reading does not say where it came from; provenance is the acquisition envelope's. A read result is recorded only inside an acquisition-batch/0 envelope, whose simulated flag the driver or simulator sets, so simulated values never look measured.\n- Device-supplied text is data and is never interpreted as instructions.\n",
    "digest": "sha256:c186793bae9310b1a6c6a7b8f62c2b9364c3d567226e7c30a2112f5391c7cb9e"
  },
  "profile": {
    "id": "Gauge-core@1",
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "GA-01",
        "summary": "Quantisation: every reading has a positive resolution; every value is an integer multiple of its resolution within 1e-9 relative."
      },
      {
        "id": "GA-02",
        "summary": "Unit consistency: value and resolution share one unit, m or rad; every reading of a stream has the unit and resolution of the first and of the gauge info in describe; every value lies within the range the gauge info declares."
      },
      {
        "id": "GA-03",
        "summary": "Zero behaviour: after a successful zero with the gauge held still the next reading is zero; zero changes neither the gauge identity, unit and resolution nor the calibration reference."
      },
      {
        "id": "GA-04",
        "summary": "Timestamp monotonicity: t_host never decreases from one reading to the next; t_dev is present in every reading or in none and increases strictly; no reading repeats an earlier one and the gauge identity and calibration reference do not change within a stream."
      },
      {
        "id": "SC-01",
        "summary": "Batch size within the recommendation: over a test stream of at least 60 s, at least 95 % of batches hold 1 MB to 8 MB or span at most 50 ms of device time."
      },
      {
        "id": "SC-02",
        "summary": "Start and stop idempotence: start_stream on a running stream changes nothing and emits no second started event; stop_stream on a stopped stream changes nothing and emits no second stopped event."
      },
      {
        "id": "SC-03",
        "summary": "Sequence contiguity: each batch starts one after the last sequence number of the batch before it; no batch range is reversed, overlapping or missing."
      },
      {
        "id": "SC-04",
        "summary": "Extension declaration and digesting: every vendor-extension setting is named under a vendor namespace listed in describe; every extension value is in the configuration digest the device reports."
      }
    ]
  }
}
